# profile P3 real-world check, 2026-10-08, Mac, scratch prod stack

## Stack
docker compose -p jobapp-p3scratch -f compose.yml -f <scratchpad>/compose.p3.yml up -d --build --wait
  (compose.p3.yml renames the images to jobapp-p3scratch-{api,caddy}:latest so the shared
  jobapp-api:latest and jobapp-caddy:latest tags are not touched; .env: APP_ENV=production,
  HTTP_PORT=8093, fresh random SECRET_KEY and database password)
  -> redis, db, api, caddy Healthy
docker compose ... exec -T api alembic upgrade head  -> 0001, 0002, 0003
docker compose ... exec -T api python -m app.identity.cli create-admin alice.p3check@example.org
docker compose ... exec -T api python -m app.identity.cli create-admin bob.p3check@example.org
  (scratch accounts; earlier scratch accounts were used by two runs that failed on the script's
  own expectations, see "Runs" below)

## Playwright through Caddy (http://127.0.0.1:8093)
uv run --native-tls --no-project --with playwright==1.55.0 --with pillow==12.3.0 \
    python tasks/evidence/profile-p3/photo_check.py <alice link file> <bob link file>
APIRequestContext for every call; Google Chrome (channel chrome, headless) for the screenshot.
The session cookie is Secure (production), so it is read from Set-Cookie and sent explicitly
over loopback http, as in P2.

