Files: exchange.json (every request and answer, headers kept: cache-control, content-type,
content-length, etag, x-content-type-options, content-disposition; secrets redacted),
downloaded-photo.jpg (the bytes GET returned), photo-in-browser.png (Chrome showing GET
/api/profile/photo: "TOP" is at the top, so the server applied EXIF orientation 6 before
stripping it; the stored file has no EXIF left for a browser to apply).

## Runs
Run 1 stopped at "GET without a photo": the script relied on the request context to send the
Secure cookie back over http, which it does not; fixed in the script (explicit Cookie header).
Run 2 reported 3 failures that were the script's own wrong expectation (683x1024 portrait; the
picture is a 3000x2000 landscape, so upright is 1024x683, which the server returned); fixed.
Run 3 (above): 0 failures.

